{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgArPCUkntz4AKSN1XE22","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HKZMrEKRxnUMqYv9vcxvbR","name":"bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-kqcpog; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('gen.py').read()\ns=s.replace('\"value\": lo, \"end\": hi','\"start\": lo, \"end\": hi')\ns=s.replace('''def build_event(plan):\n    return {''','''def describe_step(step):\n    \"\"\"One line of Intervals' text grammar: m = minutes, % LTHR for HR.\"\"\"\n    label = step.get(\"label\", \"\").strip()\n    if label[:1].isdigit():\n        raise ValueError(\"label must not start with a digit: \" + label)\n    lo, hi = step[\"hr_pct\"]\n    return \"- %s %dm %d-%d%% LTHR\" % (label, step[\"minutes\"], lo, hi)\n\n\ndef build_description(plan):\n    lines = []\n    for block in plan[\"steps\"]:\n        if \"repeat\" in block:\n            lines += [\"\", \"%dx\" % block[\"repeat\"]]\n            lines += [describe_step(s) for s in block[\"steps\"]]\n            lines.append(\"\")\n        else:\n            lines.append(describe_step(block))\n    return \"\\\\n\".join(lines).strip() + \"\\\\n\"\n\n\ndef build_event(plan):\n    return {''')\ns=s.replace('''        \"workout_doc\": build_doc(plan),''','''        \"description\": build_description(plan),\n        \"workout_doc\": build_doc(plan),''')\nopen('gen.py','w').write(s)\nE\npython3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json | head -30\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# HR corridor fix\n\n**Cause:** `gen.py` emitted HR targets as `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}`. In Intervals' FIT export, `value`+`end` is routed as a Lap-HR / zone-mapped target, so the watch clamped each corridor to its own zones (the pattern in `readback/watch-notes.md`). The API accepts it either way, which is why the readback looked fine.\n\n**Changes (`gen.py`):**\n- `hr_target` now emits `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`. `start` makes it an Instant-HR corridor, so the watch shows the raw bpm Intervals computes from its stored LTHR (172 × 75–82% = 129–141). Still percentages, not absolute bpm.\n- The event now also carries a top-level `description` in Intervals' text grammar (`- Warm-up easy 10m 68-75% LTHR`, with blank lines around `3x` repeat blocks). Without it the web UI doesn't show the steps. It uses `m` for minutes, rejects labels starting with a digit, and uses no bare `Z<n>`.\n\n**Not verified:** I couldn't push or sync a watch. The `start`/`end` shape and the description grammar come from the guide, not a live test. Re-push the event, read it back (`workout_doc.steps` must be non-empty; `[]` means the description failed to parse), then check the watch shows 117–129 / 151–160 / 129–141 / 112–124. Delete the old event 184233 first.\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1668,"cache_read_input_tokens":22299,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1668},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50c681d7-f2f5-4c15-8023-482ead47c100","uuid":"ff95aea1-8a8e-49ce-abaa-9c06dbcea7a0","timestamp":"2026-10-19T03:02:57.003Z","request_id":"req_011CgArPCDPNzqoopJ1yU3dW","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01HKZMrEKRxnUMqYv9vcxvbR":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-kqcpog; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('gen.py').read()\ns=s.replace('\"value\": lo, \"end\": hi','\"start\": lo, \"end\": hi')\ns=s.replace('''def build_event(plan):\n    return {''','''def describe_step(step):\n    \"\"\"One line of Intervals' text grammar: m = minutes, % LTHR for HR.\"\"\"\n    label = step.get(\"label\", \"\").strip()\n    if label[:1].isdigit():\n        raise ValueError(\"label must not start with a digit: \" + label)\n    lo, hi = step[\"hr_pct\"]\n    return \"- %s %dm %d-%d%% LTHR\" % (label, step[\"minutes\"], lo, hi)\n\n\ndef build_description(plan):\n    lines = []\n    for block in plan[\"steps\"]:\n        if \"repeat\" in block:\n            lines += [\"\", \"%dx\" % block[\"repeat\"]]\n            lines += [describe_step(s) for s in block[\"steps\"]]\n            lines.append(\"\")\n        else:\n            lines.append(describe_step(block))\n    return \"\\\\n\".join(lines).strip() + \"\\\\n\"\n\n\ndef build_event(plan):\n    return {''')\ns=s.replace('''        \"workout_doc\": build_doc(plan),''','''        \"description\": build_description(plan),\n        \"workout_doc\": build_doc(plan),''')\nopen('gen.py','w').write(s)\nE\npython3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json | head -30\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# HR corridor fix\n\n**Cause:** `gen.py` emitted HR targets as `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}`. In Intervals' FIT export, `value`+`end` is routed as a Lap-HR / zone-mapped target, so the watch clamped each corridor to its own zones (the pattern in `readback/watch-notes.md`). The API accepts it either way, which is why the readback looked fine.\n\n**Changes (`gen.py`):**\n- `hr_target` now emits `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`. `start` makes it an Instant-HR corridor, so the watch shows the raw bpm Intervals computes from its stored LTHR (172 × 75–82% = 129–141). Still percentages, not absolute bpm.\n- The event now also carries a top-level `description` in Intervals' text grammar (`- Warm-up easy 10m 68-75% LTHR`, with blank lines around `3x` repeat blocks). Without it the web UI doesn't show the steps. It uses `m` for minutes, rejects labels starting with a digit, and uses no bare `Z<n>`.\n\n**Not verified:** I couldn't push or sync a watch. The `start`/`end` shape and the description grammar come from the guide, not a live test. Re-push the event, read it back (`workout_doc.steps` must be non-empty; `[]` means the description failed to parse), then check the watch